COPYRIGHTS AND PROVENANCE OF THE DATA DISTRIBUTED WITH OR BY THE mlcvi PACKAGE
=============================================================================

This file lists every dataset bundled in the package (data/, inst/extdata/)
and the one file fetched on demand from OSF, with what is known about its
source, how it was derived, and its license or permission status.
Entries marked UNKNOWN could not be verified from the package sources or
the authors' public OSF archive and must be cleared before release.

Package code: GPL (>= 3), copyright the package authors (see DESCRIPTION).

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Hofstede_dims  (data/Hofstede_dims.rda; inst/extdata/Hofstede_scores_updated.csv)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Content:    National scores on Hofstede's six cultural dimensions (pdi, idv,
            mas, uai, ltowvs, ivr) for 111 entries, with ISO alpha-3 codes.
Source:     Hofstede's published national dimension scores. The CSV was
            supplied to the package by the authors; the exact release/version
            and download date are UNKNOWN.
Derivation: None beyond ISO code cleaning (data-raw/make_hofstede_data.R).
Rights:     Hofstede's dimension data are published by Geert Hofstede BV /
            Hofstede Insights. Redistribution terms: UNKNOWN. Permission to
            redistribute in this package: UNKNOWN.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Shulgin_csv  (data/Shulgin_csv.rda; inst/extdata/Shulgin.csv)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Content:    60 x 60 table of pairwise values between countries (ISO alpha-3).
            Note: the table is not symmetric (98% of cells differ from their
            transpose) and its diagonal is non-zero; whether it is a
            directional measure by design or was mis-constructed is UNKNOWN.
Source:     UNKNOWN. The package documents it as "Shulgin et al." but no
            reference, DOI, or file origin is recorded anywhere in the
            repository or the OSF archive.
Derivation: ISO code cleaning and numeric coercion (data-raw/make_shulgin_data.R).
Rights:     UNKNOWN.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. MLCVI_distance_matrix  (data/MLCVI_distance_matrix.rda; inst/extdata/MLCVI_distance_matrix.rds)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Content:    98 x 98 symmetric matrix of ML-CVI cultural distances, zero
            diagonal, ISO alpha-3 dimnames.
Source:     Produced by the package authors from the ML-CVI model.
Derivation: Computed from the country-level ML-CVI values (OSF archive
            fmduv, "Study 1_MLCVI Values_by_country.xlsx", 98 countries x 60
            items). The script and distance metric that turn those values
            into this matrix are not in the repository or the OSF archive:
            UNKNOWN (requested from the authors).
Rights:     Package authors. Underlying survey data: see entry 9.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. MLCVI_3A, MLCVI_4A  (data/MLCVI_3A.rda, data/MLCVI_4A.rda; data-raw/Study 3a_Data.xlsx, Study 4a_Data.xlsx)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Content:    Individual-level questionnaire responses: Study 3a (201
            respondents, US vs Mexico, COVID outcomes) and Study 4a (208
            respondents, US vs India, environmental behaviour), including the
            60 ML-CVI items, several published scales, and demographics.
Source:     Surveys run by the package authors; also posted in the authors'
            public OSF archive (osf.io/fmduv, folders "Study 3a", "Study 4a").
Derivation: Read from the Excel files by data-raw/make_study_datasets.R.
Rights:     Package authors. Ethics approval reference, consent terms for
            public data sharing, and whether the demographic columns are
            sufficiently de-identified for CRAN distribution: UNKNOWN.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. mlcvi_items_default, mlcvi_weights_default  (data/*.rda)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Content:    The 60 World Values Survey variable names of the ML-CVI scale and
            their dropout-loss importance weights.
Source:     ML-CVI training pipeline (OSF archive fmduv, MLScripts
            1.3.world_values_analysis.R, DALEX variable_importance); the item
            list equals the first 60 entries of
            Intermediary_files/ABCD_features.txt in that archive.
Derivation: As above; no further processing in this package.
Rights:     Package authors (derived quantities). Variable names are WVS
            codebook identifiers.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. preProcessModel_default  (data/preProcessModel_default.rda)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Content:    caret preProcess object (method = "range") fitted on the ML-CVI
            training matrix.
Source:     ML-CVI training pipeline (OSF archive fmduv, MLScripts
            1.2.world_values_model_building.R).
Rights:     Package authors.

