9. ML-CVI training matrix  (inst/extdata/train_input_matrix_small.rds, bundled;
   train_input_matrix.rds, 280,617,660 bytes, fetched from https://osf.io/download/st3hd/
   in OSF project https://osf.io/3csbz/, MD5 81ad00e3cf1d5a6c28603ac3cc9fbc6b)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Content:    Full matrix: 313,856 respondents x 594 variables (582 WVS items
            plus one-hot wave indicators s002_1..s002_6 and six derived
            *_co columns), values min-max scaled to [0, 1], no missing
            values. Bundled subsample: 2,450 rows (25 per country) drawn from
            the full matrix, with a row_indices attribute.
Source:     World Values Survey longitudinal file, release dated 2019-04-29
            (WorldValuesSurvey20190429.dta), waves 1-6, 98 countries, per
            MLScripts 1.1 in the OSF archive.
Derivation: (MLScripts 1.1) negative WVS codes set to missing; variables
            dropped/one-hot encoded per Variables_to_keep_2019-11-05.xlsx;
            90/10 train/unseen split (caTools::sample.split, seed 101);
            missing values imputed with missRanger (100 trees, 15
            iterations, extratrees split rule). (MLScripts 1.2) variables
            dropped per Delete_Before_ABCD; caret preProcess "range" scaling.
            The distributed matrix is therefore an IMPUTED and RESCALED
            derivative of WVS microdata, not the raw survey responses.
            The subsample was drawn by the package authors (script not in the
            repository: UNKNOWN).
Rights:     WVS data are provided by the World Values Survey Association
            under its data-use conditions (registration, citation, no
            redistribution of the original files is the usual condition).
            Whether redistribution of an imputed, rescaled, respondent-level
            derivative (bundled subsample and OSF file) is permitted under
            the WVS conditions applicable to the 2019-04-29 release: UNKNOWN.
            This must be confirmed with the WVS Association or replaced by
            country-level aggregates before release.

